From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: one window per Mac display

In full screen every other Mac display gets a full-screen window (its own
Space) showing the next virtio-gpu output, at that display's size, scale and
refresh rate; displays plugged in or out come and go live, and leaving full
screen closes them. The guest agrees and says where its outputs are over the
virtio port org.omacvm.display (socket at OMACVM_DISPLAY_SOCKET); the one
virtio tablet then points into the right output. OMACVM_TEST_SKIP_DISPLAYS and
OMACVM_TEST_MAIN_DISPLAY test it on virtual displays without full screen
or focus. A drag keeps the pointer while it crosses the strip between two
displays (the menu bar above a full-screen window); it lets go after the
button-up if that lands outside every window. An extra output is sized and
placed from its window once that is in full screen. The layout names the
output on the Mac's built-in display ("builtin"), which Omanotch follows.

Upstream: not applicable (OmacVM's own guest port and layout).
Test: a real external monitor above a notch MacBook: one output per display
at native size, the macOS arrangement, pointer within 0.1 point on both,
typing on both, Cmd-drag of a window across 6 of 6, plug and unplug by
mirroring. Applies after qemu-cocoa-modifiers-input-only.patch.
